From adae619c0fa0b23d5c81ad811d83e5a7598bdf8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:58:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(finalize): no root password outside QEMU

0001 set mkosi.conf's RootPassword to a SHA-512 hash of "marathon" for
every image, so each phone image let anyone with a console or a
password prompt in as root with a published password, and base trees
built before it had an empty root password with su installed.

Lock root's password in finalize for every device but QEMU, whose
serial harness logs in with it. The field becomes "*", not "!":
OpenSSH without UsePAM (Alpine's default) refuses even key logins to
an account whose hash starts with "!", which would shut out
developer images' MARATHON_DEV_SSH_KEY; "*" matches no password and
leaves key login alone.
---
 mkosi.finalize | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mkosi.finalize b/mkosi.finalize
index 255295a..fa3e496 100755
--- a/mkosi.finalize
+++ b/mkosi.finalize
@@ -99,6 +99,14 @@ while IFS=: read -r group _ _ members; do
     done
 done < "$BUILDROOT/etc/group"
 
+# mkosi.conf's RootPassword is the known hash the QEMU harness logs in
+# with. Elsewhere root takes no password; "*" rather than "!", which sshd
+# without UsePAM treats as locked and so refuses a developer image's key.
+case "$PMOS_DEVICE" in
+qemu-*) ;;
+*) sed -i 's|^root:[^:]*:|root:*:|' "$BUILDROOT/etc/shadow" ;;
+esac
+
 # Build the base confext from /etc.
 # NOTE: This next section *moves* /etc in the buildroot, so anything that
 # follows this should not expect /etc to be populated!
-- 
2.55.0

